The price went down → stop losses were triggered → longs with leverage started to close → liquidations followed → the market fell even harder. A classic cascade.
The reasons are simple and familiar:
— the market was overloaded with longs;
— large players took profits;
— against the backdrop of general nervousness, money is leaving risk.

